<title>USA: Minn. committee alters Twins stadium bill - paper.</title>
<headline>Minn. committee alters Twins stadium bill - paper.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Minnesota Senate committee has revised a bill for a new stadium for the Minnesota Twins baseball team by eliminating public funding for the project and increasing the team's contribution, the Star Tribune reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Senate Commitee on Local and Metropolitan Government approved the revised bill on Monday even though it now contains no public revenue sources, the paper said.</p>
<p>A member of the Pohlad Family, which owns the team and which has offered to contribute $15 million to the project as well as give the state a 49 percent stake in the team, reportedly said the revised bill will not work.</p>
<p>The stadium is expected to cost $250 million to $300 million or more if a retractable roof is added.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
